id: crm
name: Customer relationship and sales
industry: Sales, marketing & service
domain: CRM: accounts, contacts, leads, opportunities, campaigns, quotes and service cases
scope: Accounts and contacts, leads and their sources, opportunities and pipeline stages, products and quotes, marketing campaigns and responses, activities, service cases and customer feedback.
summary: Describes how a business wins and keeps customers: who they are, how interest becomes an opportunity and a deal, which campaigns produced it, and how customers are served afterwards. A starter model for sales pipeline, marketing attribution and service analytics.
purpose: Shared vocabulary across CRM, marketing automation and service desk tools.
read: A Lead comes from a Lead source or Campaign and may convert into an Account, Contact and Opportunity. An Opportunity moves through Sales stages, is owned by a Sales rep, and is priced with a Quote of Quote lines for Products. Activities record interactions. After the sale, Service cases and Feedback record how the customer is looked after.
in: Accounts and contacts; Leads and campaigns; Opportunities, quotes; Activities; Service cases and feedback
out: Order fulfilment; Invoicing and collections; Product catalogue management; Web analytics detail
std: schema | high | Organisations, people, products and offers are aligned to schema.org. | schema:Organization, schema:Person, schema:Product, schema:Offer
std: crmcustomer | medium | Party names, addresses and relationships follow OASIS CIQ. | Party, PartyName, Address, PartyRelationship
std: gr | low | Offer and price concepts follow GoodRelations. | gr:Offering, gr:PriceSpecification
std: vcard | low | Contact details follow the vCard ontology. | vcard:hasEmail, vcard:hasTelephone
== Customer | Accounts and contacts | Who we sell to.
Account | A company or household that is a customer or prospect. | ~schema:Organization
  - account number : string !
  - name : string !
  - industry : string
  - annual revenue : decimal
  - city : string
  - country : string
  > owned by > SalesRep ?
  > in segment > Segment ?
  > has type > AccountType 1
AccountType | The relationship with the account.
  * Prospect, Customer, Partner, Former customer
Segment | A grouping of accounts for targeting.
  * Enterprise, Mid-market, Small business, Consumer
Contact | A person at an account. | ~schema:Person
  - name : string !
  - job title : string
  - email : string
  - phone : string
  - opted out : boolean
  > works for > Account 1 | | has contact
SalesRep | A person responsible for selling.
  - employee number : string !
  - name : string !
  > in territory > Territory ?
Territory | A geographic or named area of sales responsibility.
  - territory name : string !
== Demand | Leads and campaigns | Where interest comes from.
Lead | An unqualified expression of interest by a person or company.
  - name : string !
  - company : string
  - email : string
  - created on : date !
  - score : integer
  > from source > LeadSource ?
  > from campaign > Campaign ?
  > has status > LeadStatus 1
  > converted to > Opportunity ?
LeadSource | The channel a lead came from.
  * Website, Referral, Event, Cold call, Partner, Advertisement, Social media
LeadStatus | The state of a lead.
  * New, Contacted, Qualified, Unqualified, Converted
Campaign | A planned marketing effort with a budget and a goal.
  - campaign name : string !
  - start date : date
  - end date : date
  - budget : decimal
  - actual cost : decimal
  > of type > CampaignType 1
CampaignType | The kind of campaign.
  * Email, Event, Webinar, Digital ads, Direct mail, Telemarketing
CampaignResponse | A contact's or lead's reaction to a campaign.
  - responded on : date !
  - response : string
  > to campaign > Campaign 1 | | has response
  > by contact > Contact ?
  > by lead > Lead ?
== Sales | Opportunities and quotes | Turning interest into deals.
Opportunity | A qualified chance to sell, with an expected value and close date.
  - opportunity name : string !
  - amount : decimal
  - probability percent : decimal
  - expected close : date
  - created on : date !
  - closed on : date
  > for account > Account 1 | | has opportunity
  > primary contact > Contact ?
  > owned by > SalesRep 1
  > at stage > SalesStage 1
  > lost for > LossReason ?
SalesStage | A step of the sales process.
  * Qualification, Needs analysis, Proposal, Negotiation, Closed won, Closed lost
LossReason | Why an opportunity was lost.
  * Price, Competitor, No budget, No decision, Product fit, Timing
Product | Something the business sells. | ~schema:Product
  - product code : string !
  - name : string !
  - list price : decimal
  - family : string
Quote | A priced proposal made for an opportunity.
  - quote number : string !
  - issued on : date !
  - valid until : date
  - total amount : decimal
  - accepted : boolean
  > for opportunity > Opportunity 1
QuoteLine | One product, quantity and price on a quote.
  - quantity : decimal !
  - unit price : decimal !
  - discount percent : decimal
  > of quote > Quote 1 | | has line
  > for product > Product 1
Activity | A call, meeting, email or task with a customer.
  - subject : string !
  - happened at : dateTime !
  - notes : string
  > of type > ActivityType 1
  > with contact > Contact ?
  > about opportunity > Opportunity ?
  > by rep > SalesRep ?
ActivityType | The kind of interaction.
  * Call, Meeting, Email, Demo, Task
== Service | Service and feedback | Looking after customers.
ServiceCase | A customer's request for help or complaint.
  - case number : string !
  - opened at : dateTime !
  - closed at : dateTime
  - subject : string
  > raised by > Contact ?
  > for account > Account 1
  > about product > Product ?
  > has priority > CasePriority 1
  > has status > CaseStatus 1
CasePriority | How urgent a case is.
  * Low, Medium, High, Critical
CaseStatus | The state of a case.
  * New, In progress, Waiting on customer, Resolved, Closed
Feedback | A customer's rating of their experience.
  - given on : date !
  - score : integer ! | For example a 0-10 recommendation score.
  - comment : string
  > from contact > Contact ?
  > about case > ServiceCase ?
rule: derivation | Weighted pipeline | Weighted pipeline is the sum of opportunity amount times probability for open opportunities. | Opportunity
rule: constraint | Loss needs reason | An opportunity at stage Closed lost must have a loss reason. | Opportunity
rule: constraint | Respect opt-out | A contact who has opted out is not included in campaigns. | Contact, Campaign
rule: derivation | Win rate | Win rate is opportunities Closed won divided by all closed opportunities. | Opportunity
uc: Pipeline by stage and rep | Sales manager | What is the open pipeline by stage and sales rep, and what closes this quarter? | Opportunity, SalesStage, SalesRep | at stage, Opportunity.owned by, Opportunity.amount, Opportunity.expected close
uc: Campaign return | Marketing manager | Which campaigns produced leads that became won opportunities, and at what cost? | Campaign, Lead, Opportunity, SalesStage | from campaign, converted to, at stage, Campaign.actual cost, Opportunity.amount
uc: Win and loss reasons | Sales operations | What is the win rate by segment, and why are deals lost? | Opportunity, Account, Segment, SalesStage, LossReason | Opportunity.for account, in segment, at stage, lost for
uc: Case resolution time | Service manager | How long do cases take to resolve, by priority and product? | ServiceCase, CasePriority, Product | ServiceCase.opened at, ServiceCase.closed at, has priority, about product
